# Humanizer

Source of truth: `.cursor/skills/humanizer/SKILL.md` (also `.agents/skills/humanizer/SKILL.md`).
When writing or editing user-facing prose (UI copy, docs, README, commit/PR body, landing text, briefs), follow that skill end to end.

## Must

1. Read the skill before rewriting prose. Do not invent a shorter private checklist.
2. Keep every supported fact, name, number, date, quote, and claim.
3. Act on §1–§5 on one sighting. Weak-alone patterns need company in the same passage.
4. Change prose only. Leave code, commands, paths, YAML/frontmatter, data, and link targets alone.
5. Korean UI/brief prose still follows `korean-prose.mdc` / `koreanProseRules.ts`. Humanizer does not override josa or 종결 규칙.

## Do not

- Pad significance ("pivotal", "landscape", "testament", "delve").
- Use not-X-but-Y, one-line closers, staged openers, or chatbot wrappers.
- Em-dash / en-dash as the default connector unless a writing sample uses them.
